# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
epictetus-2.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 2 ways: epictetus-2.logic.r1 and epictetus-2.logic.r1.2 have "place_with_virtue → inclines_virtue" and "¬place_with_virtue → inclines_interest_only"; epictetus-2.logic.r1.3 has "□(place_with_virtue → inclines_virtue)" and "□(¬place_with_virtue → inclines_interest_only)"; they differ when only "a man puts in the same place his interest, sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends", "the animal inclines toward sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, because the I and the Mine are placed with them", "the animal inclines toward interest alone, because the I and the Mine are placed apart from these" and "necessarily, (if a man puts in the same place his interest, sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, then the animal inclines toward sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, because the I and the Mine are placed with them)" are true, which the first allows
epictetus-2.md:1: argue/modal-ambiguous: S2 is read epictetus-2.logic.r1 and epictetus-2.logic.r1.2 with no modality; epictetus-2.logic.r1.3 as what is necessary or possible: the text does not say which it means [in 1 of 2 runs]
epictetus-2.md:1: argue/answered: S2: answered no, which keeps epictetus-2.logic.r1.3, to: Suppose "a man puts in the same place his interest, sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends", "the animal inclines toward sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, because the I and the Mine are placed with them", "the animal inclines toward interest alone, because the I and the Mine are placed apart from these" and "necessarily, (if a man puts in the same place his interest, sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, then the animal inclines toward sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, because the I and the Mine are placed with them)" are true and "necessarily, (if it is not so that a man puts in the same place his interest, sanctity, goodness, country, parents and friends, then the animal inclines toward interest alone, because the I and the Mine are placed apart from these)" is false. Is S2, "For where the I and the Mine are placed, to that place of necessity the animal inclines; if in the flesh, there is the ruling power; if in the will, it is there; and if it is in externals, it is there.", true then?
